The GFIT4C program (CPC program library catalogue number: ADNB) consists of the 
following files:

README:         This file.

gfit4c.f:       Fortran code file.

dimensions.inc: Parameter instructions to be included in compilation time.

gfit4c.sh:      driver exec file in unix shell format. It compiles gfit4c.f 
                and runs the test run.

gfit4c.inp:     the test run input file.

gfit4c.out:     the test run output file.

fitout.f:       the test run output fortran program file.


All the files are given in UNIX tar format as a single file named "gfit4c.tar", 
to extract them in a single directory execute the "tar" command at your own
UNIX installation (example: "tar -xvf gfit4c.tar"). Once all the files are 
extracted, change to executable the file "gfit4c.sh" ("chmod +x gfit4c.sh") and
execute it by typing its name ("gfit4c.sh") to run the test (it will take several
CPU hours). You can compare the output produced at your installation ("output" 
file) with the "gfit4c.out" file.

